WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
When we talk about contemporary Turkey we think&nbsp;
of the long career of the current president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.160
Erdogan. But we will come slowly to talk about his&nbsp;
politics. First a little geography, which never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.760
hurts. We are dealing with a nation in the middle&nbsp;
between Southeastern Europe and Western Asia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:21.920
divided into two peninsular regions: Eastern&nbsp;
Thrace and Anatolia, bordered to the northwest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:28.000
by Greece and Bulgaria, to the south by Syria&nbsp;
and Iraq, and to the east by Iran, Armenia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.360
and Georgia. Thanks to its strategic location,&nbsp;
the country has positioned itself as a bridge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:39.200
between different cultures, benefiting from&nbsp;
democratic influences from the Old Continent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.360
and becoming a role model for all Middle Eastern&nbsp;
countries aspiring to a synthesis of Islam and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.640
rule of law. Now we are witnessing a reversal,&nbsp;
and the recent authoritarian drift has greatly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:56.480
slowed down the process of establishing democratic&nbsp;
principles. We can say that the beginning of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:02.960
processes dates back to the late 19th century when&nbsp;
competition with European powers led some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:09.040
cultural elites within the Ottoman Empire to push&nbsp;
for modernization. A goal that according to some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:14.560
could be achieved by maintaining a synthesis&nbsp;
between Islamic faith and state institutions, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:20.400
which according to others, including the famous&nbsp;
Moustafa Kemal, required a clean break between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.360
state and religion, which had to be limited to&nbsp;
the private sphere of the citizen. Thus, after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:31.520
the 1923 elections that saw the victory of the&nbsp;
Republican People's Party (CHP) led by Ataturk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.960
Turkish became the official language in place&nbsp;
of Arabic, the form of state was revised in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:42.160
republican key, a head of state and a prime&nbsp;
minister appointed by the head of state were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:47.280
established. Then within the following year, to&nbsp;
solve the problem of the difficult coexistence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:53.200
between democracy and Islam, Islam was erased&nbsp;
from the country's daily life by abolishing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:59.520
sultanate, caliphate, and Islamic courts. This&nbsp;
wasn t such a clean exit, however, since despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:05.760
the forced secularization, Sunni Islam continued&nbsp;
to remain very deeply rooted, especially among the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.440
rural and less educated population, also thanks&nbsp;
to the influence that religious brotherhoods have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.960
always exerted on every aspect of society.&nbsp;
These include the Sufi-oriented Nak?ibendi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:22.640
to which Necmettin Erbakan, Erdogan's political&nbsp;
father, belonged, and the Hizmet, founded by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:28.320
Fethullah Gulen, which Erdogan used to rise to&nbsp;
power and with which he came into open conflict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:34.320
during the attempted coup of 2016. However, what&nbsp;
were the highlights of the Kemalist reforms?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:40.960
With the establishment of the Republic of Turkey&nbsp;
on October 29, 1923, legislative and executive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:46.160
powers passed into the hands of the Assembly,&nbsp;
which was responsible for electing the President&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:52.320
of the Republic, the head of the sole party, for&nbsp;
4-year terms. The head of state in turn appointed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:57.120
the president of the council of ministers and&nbsp;
the members of the council itself. Completing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.640
the picture were the stated independence of the&nbsp;
judiciary, the recognition of the formal equality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:08.400
of citizens before the law, and the granting of&nbsp;
the active and passive vote to women. A milestone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:15.280
achieved in 1934, long before several European&nbsp;
countries. But it was in 1937 that the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:21.040
important constitutional reform took place: the&nbsp;
one that defined the so-called 6 arrows of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:28.240
Turkish state: republican, nationalist, populist,&nbsp;
statist, reformist and secular. Ataturk's death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.840
in 1938 and the shift from single party to&nbsp;
multiple political formations, caused by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:39.360
a number of adverse circumstances including&nbsp;
economic backwardness compared to the West,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:44.480
were two of the main reasons that prevented&nbsp;
full democratic transition. As the years passed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:49.920
there was the emergence of more liberal currents&nbsp;
promoting private initiative that met with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:55.440
support of the dissatisfied middle class and&nbsp;
less literate rural classes. Among these,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:01.520
gaining the most support was Adnan Menderes'&nbsp;
Demokrat Parti, which, in the 1950 elections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:07.280
succeeded in ousting the old single party and&nbsp;
demolishing the pillars of Kemalism. Measures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:12.960
such as the call to prayer in Arabic, the opening&nbsp;
of many mosques, and the reading via state radio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:18.800
of passages from the Koran would allow religious&nbsp;
values to re-emerge, in contrast to the previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:24.080
statist vision. The situation is also very similar&nbsp;
in contemporary Turkey: on the one hand the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:30.320
aspiration for a secular and democratic society as&nbsp;
stated in the Constitution but on the other hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:35.120
a deeply religious society that struggles&nbsp;
to recognize itself in national democratic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:40.240
institutions. Despite the new government's&nbsp;
good achievements, including membership in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:46.480
the International Monetary Fund, openness to both&nbsp;
the West and Arab countries, and decent economic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:50.560
growth (9 percent annually), social tensions&nbsp;
simmering in the background erupted in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:57.520
famous Istanbul pogrom of 1955, when a right-wing&nbsp;
nationalist group clashed with a Greek minority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:03.360
present in the city's suburbs, resulting in the&nbsp;
deaths of 30 people. Menderes' party was accused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:09.440
of taking an authoritarian turn and planning the&nbsp;
pogrom despite its declared democratic openness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:15.120
So to restore order and prevent a religious drift&nbsp;
in the country, the army, as the guardian of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:22.560
Constitution, seized power by force on May 27,&nbsp;
1960. This date frames the first of four military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:29.520
coups in the period between 1960 and 1997, during&nbsp;
which the secular organs of the state, represented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:35.280
by the military, several times came face to face&nbsp;
against the confessional parties. An important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:42.160
step is found in the second coup of 1971 but&nbsp;
especially the third in 1980, because they served&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:47.760
to inaugurate the so-called "Turkish-Islamic&nbsp;
synthesis," that is, the fusion of Kemalism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:52.960
and Sunni Islam. In essence, the military, in&nbsp;
order to prevent the secularity of the state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:58.480
from being compromised, decided to come to an&nbsp;
agreement with the Islamic components of society,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:02.960
becoming the bridge for Islam to officially&nbsp;
penetrate the institutions. To make a long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:08.800
story short, the situation in the 1980s was this:&nbsp;
after the coup was over, a consulting assembly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:14.800
formed by the supreme military organ (the National&nbsp;
Security Council) and constitutionalist experts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:20.000
was charged with drafting the Constitution.&nbsp;
It stated the democratic and secular nature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.200
of the Turkish state, confirmed the role of&nbsp;
the supreme military organ as the protector&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:30.240
of social order, and expanded the powers of the&nbsp;
government and the President of the Republic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:37.360
The new electoral law then set the threshold for&nbsp;
entering Parliament at 10%, so that in 1983 only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:40.800
3 parties competed for seats: the People's Party&nbsp;
(Halk i Parti - direct successor to the CHP), the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:45.280
Nationalist Party (Mhp) and the Motherland&nbsp;
Party (Anap). The latter was supported by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:52.400
brotherhoods and founded by Turgut zal, who won 45&nbsp;
percent of the seats and became the ruling party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:57.280
Ozal's party succeeded in embodying that&nbsp;
Turkish-Islamic synthesis I mentioned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:02.720
bringing together the military, the brotherhoods,&nbsp;
and the small and medium business class. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:08.400
persistent economic backwardness combined with&nbsp;
corruption and inefficiency in the state began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.920
to foster the emergence of the Welfare Party&nbsp;
(Refah Partisi) founded by Erbakan in 1987 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:19.600
in which a young Erdo?an was beginning to make his&nbsp;
mark. The party wasn't driven by any particular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:24.720
ideology but, through a team of economists,&nbsp;
tried to come up with the best solutions to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:29.600
the problem of the broken state finances.&nbsp;
It was an effort that paid off, as in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:36.240
1994 local government elections the party won in&nbsp;
more than 20 municipalities, including Istanbul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:42.080
where Erdogan was elected mayor, and in&nbsp;
the July 1996 general elections Erbakan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:47.840
crowned his dream of becoming prime minister. But&nbsp;
before long, Erbakan would be way over his head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:53.520
as conservative policies implemented by his&nbsp;
local administrators began to anger the military;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:58.880
these included plans to build a mosque in&nbsp;
Istanbul's Taksim Square, a place symbolic of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:04.880
the Western way of life, and a desire to convert&nbsp;
the former St. Sophia basilica into a mosque,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:10.960
another symbol of Turkey's secular tradition&nbsp;
since it had been turned into a museum in 1934 by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:17.040
the will of Atat rk himself. In addition, contacts&nbsp;
between the Welfare Party and other Middle Eastern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:22.720
Islamic groups such as the Palestinian Hamas,&nbsp;
the Muslim Brotherhood in Egypt, and the Algerian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:27.840
Islamic Salvation Front were putting the party&nbsp;
in a bad light in the eyes of the military. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:33.600
here we come to the fourth coup of 1997, also&nbsp;
called the "post-modern" coup because it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:39.440
implemented without bloodshed, with Erbakan banned&nbsp;
from political life, accused of stealing public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:45.600
funds and inciting religious hate. The Welfare&nbsp;
Party was dismantled and in its place was born the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:51.040
following year the Virtue Party, into which the&nbsp;
young Erdogan joined even though shortly before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:56.640
he had been sentenced to 10 months in prison. And&nbsp;
given his excellent record as mayor of Istanbul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:01.840
it's not surprising that much of the population&nbsp;
considered his detention an injustice that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:07.440
have made him even more charming. Anyway, of the&nbsp;
originally planned 10 months, Erdogan served only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:13.360
four since in 2001 the Turkish Constitutional&nbsp;
Court granted amnesty to Virtue Party members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:18.320
who had been banned from public office. At&nbsp;
that point, the party split into two fronts:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:21.520
the conservative wing of the Islamic matrix&nbsp;
(Saadet Partisi - Party of Happiness) and the wing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:26.960
of the so-called innovators, the young moderate&nbsp;
reformists, of which Erdogan became the leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.640
founding the Justice and Development Party (Adalet&nbsp;
ve Kalkinma Partisi - AKP) on August 14 of that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:37.600
year. In the November 3, 2002 elections, the AKP&nbsp;
became the first party with 34.3 percent of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:43.200
vote, but for some reasons that I will not go into&nbsp;
here, Erdogan had to lead from behind the scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:49.040
letting his loyal right-hand man Abdullah&nbsp;
Gul replace him as prime minister. The AKP,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:53.520
on the strength of its policy proposals&nbsp;
aimed at reviving the country's economic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:59.680
situation hit by the 2001 crisis and rising&nbsp;
inflation, would set up a Muslim government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:05.520
inspired by European democracies but with a&nbsp;
Sunni Islamic emphasis. As Gul himself said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:10.480
"Although some of us are religiously oriented&nbsp;
individuals, we don't want to be defined as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:15.280
religious party. [...] We want to prove that&nbsp;
a Muslim-majority country can be democratic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:19.920
transparent and compatible with the modern&nbsp;
world." Major achievements in the early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:25.920
2000s including economic growth of 5 percent&nbsp;
annually, diversification of foreign trade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:31.120
and an aid program for the poorer sections of&nbsp;
the population projected Turkey into the role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:36.880
of a regional power, making it a viable candidate&nbsp;
for entry into the European Union, so much so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:43.040
negotiations reopened as early as October&nbsp;
2005. Dear Erdogan, if last year you hadn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:48.240
confined Ursula Von Der Leyen to that little couch&nbsp;
maybe your flag would also be in Brussels today.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:54.720
Jokes aside, internally the reform of the&nbsp;
National Security Council was important,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.720 --> 00:11:00.560
remember? The supreme military organ, which was&nbsp;
downgraded to an advisory organ, thus lessening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:06.640
the military's grip on institutions. In short, a&nbsp;
series of achievements that led the AKP to prevail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:14.400
in the July 22, 2007 elections with as many as&nbsp;
46.6 percent of votes in favor corresponding to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:20.240
341 seats. But on balance, the most important&nbsp;
achievement for the Turkish leader was that of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:25.520
having succeeded in getting Gul elected to&nbsp;
the position of President of the Republic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:31.120
which had in fact consolidated his power over the&nbsp;
opposition. The situation that had been created,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:35.520
however, was a harbinger of a dangerous&nbsp;
authoritarian drift because the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:40.320
would be able to push through laws bordering&nbsp;
on constitutional legitimacy without the head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:45.840
of state casting any kind of veto. Starting&nbsp;
in 2008, a number of events threatened to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:51.440
compromise the prime minister's career forever.&nbsp;
First and foremost, the law restoring the veil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:56.560
for women in universities almost cost the&nbsp;
party closure for "antilaic activities,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.560 --> 00:12:00.960
according to the dossier submitted by the&nbsp;
chief prosecutor of the Turkish Supreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:05.280
Court (Abdurrahman Yal inkaya). The rescue came&nbsp;
when the Constitutional Court, called to rule on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:10.640
the issue, initially declared the law contrary to&nbsp;
the Constitution but a few months later reversed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:15.520
itself on public interest grounds. Then it was&nbsp;
the turn of the prime minister's very strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:21.200
reaction against the members of the Ergenekon,&nbsp;
an alleged Kemalist-style secret organization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:26.160
composed mainly of senior army officials,&nbsp;
established with the aim of overthrowing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:31.360
government and seizing power in a coup. However,&nbsp;
an affair that remains unclear to this day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:36.960
with many accusing Erdo?an himself of organizing&nbsp;
everything to dispose of his political opponents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:42.640
A 2016 ruling would partially confirm these&nbsp;
fears by releasing most of those convicted.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:48.960
Finally, it was in May 2013 that there was a harsh&nbsp;
crackdown on environmentalist protests against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:54.480
construction of a shopping mall in the green area&nbsp;
of Gezi Park near Taksim Square. On that occasion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:59.760
police intervened against the protesters using&nbsp;
tear gas and water cannons. The media and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:05.360
newspapers loyal to the government tried to cover&nbsp;
up the news, but this caused the event to resonate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:10.240
even more through social networks such as Facebook&nbsp;
and Twitter, which were blacked out. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:15.760
the turbulent situation that had been created was&nbsp;
not enough to undermine the popularity of Erdogan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:21.280
who, having reached the 3-term limit and unable&nbsp;
to run again for the leadership of the government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:27.280
ran for the presidency of the Republic in 2014&nbsp;
and won with 52 percent of the votes in favor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:32.400
At that point, the "New Turkey" project desired&nbsp;
by the president required annihilating the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:38.000
internal opponent still capable of challenging&nbsp;
him. I am referring to that Fethullah Gulen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:43.360
who had long ago helped him get rid of the&nbsp;
Kemalists and who, after the Gezi Park affair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:49.120
had instead obstructed him. His brotherhood, let s&nbsp;
remember: the Hizmet, was from then on branded as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:49.920
terrorist (Terrorist Organization of the Followers&nbsp;
of Fethullah" - Fetullah i Ter r rg t ) and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:54.960
targeted by government forces. The democratic&nbsp;
values that had brought the ruling party to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.960 --> 00:14:00.960
prominence back in 2002 had been betrayed, with&nbsp;
a society sharply divided between supporters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:06.320
opponents of the regime and a president with&nbsp;
little tolerance for his enemies. Frequent was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:12.880
the use of Article 299 of the Turkish Penal Code,&nbsp;
which provided for imprisonment for all those who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:17.920
offended the president of the republic; a&nbsp;
measure that among other things in 2021 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:23.074
declared by the European Court of Human Rights to&nbsp;
be detrimental to freedom of expression (Article&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.074 --> 00:14:28.000
10 ECHR). The authoritarian drift was so obvious&nbsp;
that even within Erdogan's own party, scorched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:34.240
earth had been made. A few years earlier, the Gezi&nbsp;
Park affair had cost the removal of loyalist Gul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:40.640
and in May 2016 trusted Prime Minister Ahmet&nbsp;
Davutoglu was also removed, due to differences in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:46.720
political views, and replaced with Binali Yldrim.&nbsp;
Boiling tensions erupted on that Friday evening,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:53.760
July 15, 2016, when a reporter from state TV&nbsp;
Trt began reading a lengthy statement from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:59.040
coup plotters announcing the seizure of power.&nbsp;
At the same time, the military had occupied the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:04.480
southern bridges over the Bosphorus in Istanbul&nbsp;
and two jets flew over the city, spreading terror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:09.600
among the population. Erdo?an declared in a live&nbsp;
video feed made from his smartphone that he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:15.200
survived the attack and called for citizens to&nbsp;
take to the streets to defend democracy. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:20.880
hours of terror; in Ankara, the parliamentary&nbsp;
headquarters was hard hit by the air force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:26.640
and reduced to a pile of rubble, but by the next&nbsp;
morning it was clear that the coup had failed, as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:32.240
army units still loyal to the president managed to&nbsp;
restore the status quo. Even today it's difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:37.760
to say who organized the coup. At first Aaron&nbsp;
Stein claimed that it was some departments of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:43.040
First and Second Armies that carried it out, along&nbsp;
with the support of elements of the Air Force,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:49.040
Navy and Coast Guard. Another article by political&nbsp;
